Z||000000||whamel||08-28-2000||10:10 PM||||My shop tells me that my heater core is leaking and this is the first time I've ever really had that problem.  I'm trying to assign priority to some of these repairs and I wanted to make sure I understand the function of the heater core and what exactly the impact of having a leaky one would be.  I am guessing from what I understand you would get little heater functionality, film on the windshield, and gunk on the interior (this is in the dash, right??  I forget and don't have my manual with me.) from the runoff.  I can deal with these three things, but is there anything else I should know about?  I am probably going to assign it a 'low' priority if there's nothing else.  I have a couple other more serious repairs to handle first.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-28-2000||10:42 PM||||It's like having a hole in the radiator. It might only be dripping now but don't count on it staying that way.<P>either way your loosing coolant. Probably more than you think.||||reg||1
Z||000002||whamel||08-28-2000||10:48 PM||||They didn't seem terribly concerned about it at the shop just yet, but they did mention that I should really get that fixed as soon as possible.  Guess I'm off to find a heater core then....and a radiator.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||08-29-2000||07:02 AM||||The heater core was the first job I did on my GT when I got it 18 months ago with hardly any mechanical skills at the time. Do it yourself and save $. Piece of cake. If you don't have a Haynes, get one. All instructions for this job are contained.<P>Marc 87GT||||reg||3
Z||000004||whamel||08-29-2000||08:29 AM||||I got a price on a new one and it wasn't as bad as I thought - I was under the impression that this was going to be pretty expensive (that's why I was holding off on doing it), but for $50 I can't pass it up.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade<BR>||||reg||1
